  "distribution": "Only the listed component sources are vendored. The Next.js website, server, package manifest and registry tooling are not included.",
  "adaptations": [
    "Button imports use the directly installed @radix-ui/react-slot instead of the aggregate radix-ui package.",
    "The dropdown entry point additionally exposes the upstream underlying radio group and radio item, with matching pixel choice styling; checkbox styling is squared.",
    "DialogContent accepts the underlying Radix content props; DialogTitle does not forward the font-only prop into the DOM.",
    "TooltipContent removes its empty non-portaled wrapper so it does not occupy layout space.",
    "The retro CSS uses the original Press Start 2P family bundled locally instead of the upstream Google Fonts request. Compact UI text uses 8px with integer line boxes; headings use 10\u201312px and unsupported Unicode uses system fallbacks.",
    "The project-local cn helper uses clsx and tailwind-merge instead of the upstream website helper and site configuration.",
    "App-specific colors, compact spacing and square window chrome are in src/styles.css; component accessibility and popup behavior use actual Radix-backed 8bitcn sources.",
    "All component icons use local integer-grid SVG shapes instead of smooth lucide symbols; lucide-react is not installed.",
    "Client-only Next.js directives are omitted because this is a local Vite WebView application.",
    "The tooltip arrow is a stepped integer-grid SVG instead of a rotated rounded arrow.",
    "Tooltip roots honor the surrounding TooltipProvider delay rather than overriding it with an extra zero-delay provider.",
    "Scrollable dropdown content, subcontent and dialog content use real outer borders instead of absolute inset border layers, preventing decoration from scrolling across labels or creating horizontal overflow."
  ],
